===Mastery Strategies===
{{MastComp|{{MastStrat|first|Machine}}|{{MastStrat|second and fifth|Collect and use|Use}}|{{MastStrat|third|Toon in run|{{CI|Yatta|name=true}}}}|{{MastStrat|fourth|Meters}}|{{MastStrat|sixth|focus on only using your Ability to yourself, as this over time will complete the task}}}}
==Requirement Strategies==
*For the first requirement, focus on picking up {{II|Baskets|name=true}} and extracting [[Machines]]. The Machine and Basket count increases the further you descend, so you can earn more Baskets.
*For the second requirement, try to play normally whilst also focusing on collecting as much [[Research]] as you can. Primarily focus on {{Type|Common}} [[Twisteds]], as they are, as their rarity implies, more common than others. Also play as {{CI|Rodger|name=true}} to make this process easier.

==Golden Skin [[Quest]]==
{{GQ|Encounter {{CI|Twisted Cocoa|name=true}} {{Color|10|#93f525}} times as Cocoa.}}
{{GQ|Complete {{Color|35|#93f525}} total [[Floors]] as Cocoa.}}
{{GQ|Use Cocoa's [[ability]] to place {{Color|40|#93f525}} {{II|BonBon|name=true|plural=a}} that are picked up by other [[Toons]].}}

Reward: {{Skin|Golden Bunny Cocoa}} [[Skin]] ''{{Small|(Exclusively obtainable while the [[Easter Event]] is active)}}''

===Golden Skin Strategies===
*'''For the first quest''', play normally until you see {{CI|Twisted Cocoa|name=true}} on the [[Floor]]. Then, either encounter her normally or ask the distractor to bring Twisted Cocoa to the Elevator. It is easier to do this when she's on the [[Daily Twisted Board]]. Additionally, you should try to reach higher Floors, since that is where {{Type|Rare}} [[Twisteds]] become more common.
*'''For the second quest''', get in a team with fast extractors such as [[Shelly]] or [[Squirm]] to pass the Floors quickly, do this multiple times to get this quest completed fast.
*'''For the third quest''', equip {{TI|Ghost Snakes In A Can|name=true}} and {{TI|Sweet Charm|name=true}} as Cocoa. Get one or more other player(s) and spam your BonBon [[Ability]] at the Elevator and have the other teammates use them. If you can't tell them that, use the {{SI|Here, for you!|name=true}} [[Sticker]]. You can also invite someone in a duo run and spam your Ability while you both are at an AFK spot of the map.

==Strategies==
Given her above average [[Movement Speed]] and [[Stealth]], Cocoa is seemingly made to lean into being a support [[Toon]] rather than a distractor or extractor. With her [[Ability]], {{AI|Cocoa|name=true}}, Cocoa is able to give other players a slight boost with the {{II|BonBons|name=true}} she drops, whether it's a boost for [[Extraction Speed]] or Movement Speed.

Placing down BonBons near players on Machines with slow [[Extraction Speed]] or when slow [[Movement Speed]] Toons are being chased is a way to help out your team, or placing down unneeded BonBons when your team doesn't need any to a {{CI|Sprout|name=true}} or a {{CI|Ginger|name=true}} is another way on using Cocoa's Ability as it helps with gathering {{Tape|name=true}} for their Abilities. Essentially, placing her BonBons next to [[Machines]] and around the map can be helpful for other players and even herself.

Remember that Cocoa's Ability can also benefit herself as well. You can use BonBons from her Ability to boost her slower Extraction Speed frequently, speeding up Floor progression. Her BonBons can also provide her with a speed boost equivalent to the boost of a {{II|Speed Candy|name=false}} for a double duration, which can help her escape chases easier, especially with her already high mobility. This can also help Cocoa conserve Stamina, which is very helpful due to her below-average [[Stamina]] capacity.

Cocoa, despite her Stealth, is capable of being a decent distractor given her BonBons' speed boost. She can place down BonBons and use them to give herself distance from faster [[Twisteds]], mitigate the {{Debuff|Slow|}} Debuff, to escape a chase when [[Panic Mode]] is active, or anything else. If planning to distract as her with ease, arrange a run with various 4{{Star}} and above Stealth Toons as it's much easier to get Twisteds off of them this way, and also equip the usual distractor [[Trinkets]], such as {{TI|Dog Plush|name=true}} and {{TI|Speedy Shoes|name=true}} or {{TI|Train Whistle|name=true}}.  If you don’t want or need to use the Trinkets suggested, her Ability is always good for speed, though note its fairly long cooldown.

Below are the values of the BonBons' Movement Speed and Extraction Speed boosts on different Star counts.
